{"task": "Implement two C11 lock-free variants of the pair API. Return exactly keys exchange_source and store_source, each a complete pair.c string. Preserve arbitrary signed 32-bit values, including INT32_MIN/MAX. Pack both values in the one supplied 64-bit atomic object; one atomic load must provide the complete snapshot. exchange_source must publish using atomic_exchange_explicit with memory_order_acq_rel; store_source must publish using atomic_store_explicit with memory_order_release. Both use atomic_load_explicit with memory_order_acquire. No mutex, helper thread, allocation, inline assembly, second shared-state object, clock operation, output, or changes to header/harness. Include pair.h and implement only the two declared functions. Do not define pair_bits: the harness owns it. No Markdown. The returned old value from exchange is not needed by this interface.", "protected_header": "#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>
extern _Atomic(uint64_t) pair_bits;
void set_pair(int32_t a, int32_t b);
void get_pair(int32_t *a, int32_t *b);
", "acceptance": "Independent protected harness checks exact arbitrary values, concurrent paired snapshot consistency, final writer values, lock-free availability, 100 stress runs, semantics, original tests and three TSan runs."}

{"exchange_source": "#include "pair.h"

void set_pair(int32_t a, int32_t b) {
    uint64_t packed = ((uint64_t)(uint32_t)a) | ((uint64_t)(uint32_t)b) << 32;
    atomic_exchange_explicit(&pair_bits, packed, memory_order_acq_rel);
}
", "store_source": "#include "pair.h"

void set_pair(int32_t a, int32_t b) {
    uint64_t packed = ((uint64_t)(uint32_t)a) | ((uint64_t)(uint32_t)b) << 32;
    atomic_store_explicit(&pair_bits, packed, memory_order_release);
}
"}
